**arbitrary** function `u : ℝ² → ℂ` of `(r, θ)` (III's coordinates, index `0 = r`, `1 = θ`), the four-dimensional
mode field is `modeField om mm u (t,r,θ,φ) = P(t,φ) u(r,θ)` with `P = exp(−iωt + imφ)` (`phaseP`; the phase
convention of Hintz arXiv:2609.33661v1 and of III). Derivatives are the complex-valued **real** slice derivatives
`cpdC` (`Atlas.EinsteinMaxwell.NP.Basic`); the frame acts by `cdir` (complex-linear combination of real partials).

Bridge to III's existing two-dimensional derivative `Hintz2026.cpd` (not a copy): `cpdC_mode_r`, `cpdC_mode_th`
(`∂_r`, `∂_θ` of the mode field are `P` times III's `cpd 0`, `cpd 1` of `u` at `toRT x = (r, θ)`), together with
`∂_t ↦ −iω`, `∂_φ ↦ im`. With `K = −(r²+a²)ω + am`, `Q̂ = −aω sinθ + m/sinθ`:

    l(P u)  = P (∂_r u + iK/Δ u)                       = P · Dop    p 0 ω m u     (every x)
    n(P u)  = P (−Δ/(2Σ)) (∂_r u − iK/Δ u)             = P (−Δ/(2Σ)) · DopDag p 0 ω m u   (Δ ≠ 0)
    m(P u)  = P/(√2 q) (∂_θ u − Q̂ u)                    = P/(√2 ρ̄) · LopDag p 0 ω m u  (every x)
    m̄(P u)  = P/(√2 q̄) (∂_θ u + Q̂ u)                    = P/(√2 ρ̄*) · Lop  p 0 ω m u   (every x)

where `Dop`, `DopDag`, `Lop`, `LopDag` are III's original definitions (`Atlas/Perturbations/Hintz2026/System1Defs.lean`)
at `j = 0`, imported unchanged. The general-parameter forms `dir_*_mode` hold for every real `M a Q` (`a = 0`, `Q = 0`
allowed); III's `SubextremalKN p` enters only in the `*_eq_Dop…` bridges. The identities need no regularity of `u`
(both sides use the same `deriv` semantics); for `u` `C^∞` (order `∞`) on III's `U p`, the mode field is `C^∞` on
`domKN` and every `cpdC` is a genuine derivative (`hasDerivAt_modeField`). `P ≠ 0`, so each frame derivative vanishes iff
the corresponding III operator does (`dir_*_eq_zero_iff`; no division by `ω` or `m`, `ω = 0`, `m = 0` included).
